  "statement": "Write a function that returns the square root of 'nb' if it is a perfect\nsquare (i.e. its root is itself a whole number representable as an int),\nand 0 otherwise. Watch out for integer overflow.",
  "allowed_functions": [],
  "harness": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint ft_sqrt(int nb);\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv)\n{\n    (void)argc;\n    printf(\"%d\", ft_sqrt(atoi(argv[1])));\n    return (0);\n}\n",
